<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>{{ .Title }}</title>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>HTMX Cross-Origin</title>
    <!-- Configure HTMX before it loads -->
    <meta name="htmx-config" content='{"selfRequestsOnly": false}'>
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/htmx.org@2.0.4"></script>
    <style>
      #body {
        font-family:arial;
      }
    </style>
</head>
<body id="body">

  <div style="width:90%;margin:0 auto;">

    <h1>{{ .Heading }}</h1>

    This is a learning project inspired by the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/ssl/lava-lamp-encryption/">Cloudflare lava lamp wall of entropy</a>.  
    Using one or more webcams, this project is able to generate real world random number rather than using regular
    random type programming libraries which aren't truly random.  The point of this project was to learn how to take real
    world entropy and distill it down into a random number.
    <br/><br/>

    <div id="filter-group">
        <input name="min" type="number" value="0" /><br/><br/>
        <input name="max" type="number" value="1000000" /><br/>
    </div>
    <br/>

    <button hx-get="http://localhost:8888/random" hx-target="#details" hx-include="#filter-group">
      Get a Random Number
    </button>
    <br/><br/>

    <div id="details">
    </div>

  </div>

</body>
</html>